(3448237, 472487, 55838, '<td valign="top">Wow Rina.  You certainly received some interesting comments here.  Apparently your shot struck some sort of emotional chord in some viewers - that''s a good thing (as annoying as some of their comments are!).  The comments got me thinking...what an incredibly broad and variable as well as subjective definition of HATE we seem to have in this world.  Sometimes HATE can be defined as mildly disagreeing with anothers lifestyle choices.  Sometimes HATE is used to describe how I feel about canned lima beans.  Sometimes HATE is defined so strongly such as when a few guys kill thousands of people who went to work in a highrise building on a normal Tuesday morning.  And as far as war is concerned, I''m no historian but I can think of no war that did not involve HATE in some way shape or form.  Not sure how a situation would come to war without some element of hatred on one side or the other.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-10 08:22:20.</i></td>', 'Wow Rina.  You certainly received some interesting comments here.  Apparently your shot struck some sort of emotional chord in some viewers - that''s a good thing (as annoying as some of their comments are!).  The comments got me thinking...what an incredibly broad and variable as well as subjective definition of HATE we seem to have in this world.  Sometimes HATE can be defined as mildly disagreeing with anothers lifestyle choices.  Sometimes HATE is used to describe how I feel about canned lima beans.  Sometimes HATE is defined so strongly such as when a few guys kill thousands of people who went to work in a highrise building on a normal Tuesday morning.  And as far as war is concerned, I''m no historian but I can think of no war that did not involve HATE in some way shape or form.  Not sure how a situation would come to war without some element of hatred on one side or the other.', '2007-03-10 08:20:23.000000', '2007-03-10 08:22:20.000000', 0),
(3456339, 472643, 35786, '<td valign="top">LOVE it!!! :0D</td>', 'LOVE it!!! :0D', '2007-03-13 12:12:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3460348, 472342, 67145, '<td valign="top">hi manish ... excellent image here .. its actually a stunner ... fantastic idea and totally amazing result .. congratulations on an 8th place and a wonderful photograph ...<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-03-14 11:53:31.</i></td>', 'hi manish ... excellent image here .. its actually a stunner ... fantastic idea and totally amazing result .. congratulations on an 8th place and a wonderful photograph ...', '2007-03-14 11:51:53.000000', '2007-03-14 11:53:31.000000', 0),
(3460397, 470720, 1031, '<td valign="top">I haven''t been to an SCA event for a long time -- good looking armor! I think you did a pretty good job of showing the fury and confusion of battle, though I''m not sure that soldiers in battle "hate" the enemy in the same way an individual might; that might have influenced the score you got.</td>', 'I haven''t been to an SCA event for a long time -- good looking armor! I think you did a pretty good job of showing the fury and confusion of battle, though I''m not sure that soldiers in battle "hate" the enemy in the same way an individual might; that might have influenced the score you got.', '2007-03-14 12:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3466303, 471924, 11843, '<td valign="top">I just read the Critique Club''s evaluation of your photo here.<br/>I don''t agree on the border. I think the border helps this photo with keeping the viewers eye from roaming outside the photo. The bars naturally lead the viewers eyes around the photo and the border keeps your eye from leaving. I also don''t think the photo is over sharpened. Animal fur unfortunately looks over sharpened when there is a higher amount of contrast like there is between the cats eyes. There are no signs, that I can see, that much sharpening has been done. You don''t see that halo around the whiskers or between the eye and eyelid that over sharpening would produce. I agree with the rest. Great shot, with a good challenge placement for a pet shot.<br/></td>', 'I just read the Critique Club''s evaluation of your photo here.I don''t agree on the border. I think the border helps this photo with keeping the viewers eye from roaming outside the photo. The bars naturally lead the viewers eyes around the photo and the border keeps your eye from leaving. I also don''t think the photo is over sharpened. Animal fur unfortunately looks over sharpened when there is a higher amount of contrast like there is between the cats eyes. There are no signs, that I can see, that much sharpening has been done. You don''t see that halo around the whiskers or between the eye and eyelid that over sharpening would produce. I agree with the rest. Great shot, with a good challenge placement for a pet shot.', '2007-03-16 10:47:41.000000', NULL, 0),
